update public.questions q
set explanation = v.e
from (values
('aee4fd41-16ae-40b2-9792-904414467356', 'Breadth-first search explores a graph level by level, so it keeps the nodes waiting to be visited in a queue (first in, first out). A stack is used by depth-first search instead.'),
('b01ae1dd-e9d0-4787-a2ba-dfb41bde7dd3', 'Integrate by parts with u = ln x and dv/dx = 1, so du/dx = 1/x and v = x. This gives x ln x − ∫ 1 dx = x ln x − x + c.'),
('b051c20a-57a7-4987-9868-db31fdbd15fe', 'The dot product of (1, 0) and (1, 1) is 1 × 1 + 0 × 1 = 1, and the magnitudes are 1 and √2. So cos θ = 1/√2, which gives θ = 45°.'),
('b0b53159-ce12-4bd1-85ad-575c4e510649', 'Angular speed is the angle in radians swept per second. One full period T covers 2π radians, so ω = 2π/T. The π/T option covers only half a turn.'),
('b0e9d699-4b69-4a57-9e44-5042398754d3', 'On a string fixed at both ends, the fundamental loop spans L = λ/2, so λ = 2L. Since v = fλ, the fundamental frequency is f = v/(2L).'),
('b15342da-92d1-4e39-9910-3e1230f64880', 'Substitute t = 1 into r = (1, 2) + t(3, −1): the point is (1 + 3, 2 − 1) = (4, 1). None of the other options matches any value of t.'),
('b18263db-732a-4cb2-8d0e-53c6cb791e2d', 'Uncompressed file size is width × height × bits per pixel = 800 × 600 × 24 = 11 520 000 bits. The 480 000 option is 800 × 600 alone, which leaves out the colour depth.'),
('b1c6cdec-4aea-4c4e-9b64-188c3b43e6b5', 'Virtual memory lets the operating system use part of the disk as an extension of RAM. Pages not currently needed are moved to disk (paging) and brought back into RAM when required.'),
('b2ac5706-7c4b-417f-8125-82b3ecc647de', 'One hex digit holds values from 0 to 15, which needs four binary digits because 2⁴ = 16. So each hex digit represents exactly 4 bits.'),
('b3cd74d5-6e4d-46c4-a3fa-efe090f83a93', 'A parabola touches the x-axis when its discriminant is zero: Δ = b² − 4ac = 16 − 4c = 0, so c = 4. Then x² + 4x + 4 = (x + 2)², a perfect square.'),
('b49bf1b1-a471-4135-bb1f-9d27f671a6ec', 'Indexed addressing calculates an effective address as a base address plus an index offset. That makes it ideal for stepping through array elements one after another.'),
('b5b7c939-a844-418c-a903-2f47314ada02', 'NOR is OR followed by NOT. For A = 0 and B = 0, OR gives 0, and inverting that gives 1. NOR is therefore 1 only when both inputs are 0.'),
('b5fc8646-2583-4776-a664-fbb27be335ff', 'In a linear queue the slots at the front are left empty after dequeues, which wastes space. A circular queue wraps the pointers round, so freed slots are reused.'),
('b6eef770-3dc4-43fd-bccf-bd5dd2755f91', 'Start from cos 2A = cos²A − sin²A and replace sin²A with 1 − cos²A. This gives cos²A − (1 − cos²A) = 2cos²A − 1.'),
('b76e32c6-dad4-4a6f-b3d4-23a58a03b652', 'When a wire is at right angles to a uniform field, F = BIL = 0.40 T × 3.0 A × 0.25 m = 0.30 N. The 3.3 N option comes from adding the values rather than multiplying them.'),
('b7f867b7-a272-415e-b98c-8713095cb2df', 'In hexadecimal, 2F means 2 × 16 + 15 = 32 + 15 = 47. The letter F stands for 15 in the units place.'),
('b97eb393-7849-40dc-8719-41a3ca204425', 'An SR latch is in an invalid state when both S and R are 1. Both outputs are then forced to 0, so Q and Q̄ are no longer complements of each other.'),
('bbdfdf46-c7cf-4b46-8db6-cecaed6c3619', 'The integral of e^(ax) is e^(ax)/a + c. With a = 3 this gives e^(3x)/3 + c. The 3e^(3x) option is what you get by differentiating instead.'),
('bbe9c1ef-eeb4-407c-b639-726699a6697d', 'In an elastic collision total momentum and total kinetic energy are both conserved, because no kinetic energy is converted into heat, sound or deformation.'),
('bc58e771-eb62-45fa-9bb5-2e08a0c7784f', 'Every value equals the mean, so each deviation from the mean is zero. The variance is therefore 0, and the standard deviation is √0 = 0.'),
('bc655b0d-f59f-4f30-88e1-7b0d24582172', 'Depth-first search follows one path as far as it can go before backtracking. It uses a stack, or equivalently recursion, to hold the path currently being explored.'),
('bcae7ed8-5752-4df8-a4bd-da77ca0b7a02', 'The variance of the sample mean is σ²/n. Doubling n gives σ²/(2n), which is half the original variance, so the multiplier is 0.5.'),
('bd13adbb-2135-4a36-8e22-f28b2d8db343', 'Power is work done divided by time: P = W/t = 500 J ÷ 10 s = 50 W. The 5000 W option multiplies the work by the time, the wrong operation.'),
('bee177ad-1ab8-4357-8fee-2dfbc12942f7', 'Merge sort divides the list in half and merges sorted halves. Its work is about n log n comparisons on average, so its average complexity is O(n log n).'),
('c104e058-13fd-45cc-95ba-437f3742d401', 'Pressure is force divided by area: p = F/A = 100 N ÷ 0.5 m² = 200 Pa. The 50 Pa option multiplies the force by the area instead of dividing.'),
('c1443aa1-09ad-4189-bc02-e01191355bfb', 'Perpendicular lines have gradients whose product is −1. The line y = 3x − 2 has gradient 3, so the perpendicular gradient is −1/3.'),
('c2670b7c-a1f9-4737-b1c6-374fbd0b87aa', 'To convert radians to degrees multiply by 180/π, so π/12 radians = (180/π) × π/12 = 180/12 = 15°.'),
('c2efecf9-e6d9-4cda-9bce-74c4409fbf31', 'A back bearing differs from the forward bearing by 180°. From B to A the bearing is 130° + 180° = 310°, which lies within the 0° to 360° range.'),
('c40fb60a-a117-4cd1-bf89-77096022e659', '|x + 3| < 2 means −2 < x + 3 < 2. Subtracting 3 from each part gives −5 < x < −1, so the answer is the interval between those values.'),
('c55d87d2-3e28-4aac-8b08-9298a1eae57d', 'The Central Limit Theorem states that for a large sample size n the sample mean is approximately normally distributed, whatever the shape of the population distribution.'),
('c5d75bfd-0d14-4834-80d4-690d67733f92', 'By the remainder theorem, the remainder when p(x) is divided by (x − 2) is p(2). Here p(2) = 2³ − 2 × 2² + 5 = 8 − 8 + 5 = 5.'),
('c80a9ebf-e985-4e48-ae69-ddd84087780f', 'Using Var(X) = E(X²) − μ² with E(X²) = 1.7 and μ = 1.1 gives 1.7 − 1.1² = 1.7 − 1.21 = 0.49.'),
('c858ab36-a860-40ad-bc71-df43b26b607f', 'Acceleration is the change in velocity divided by the time taken: a = (30 − 0) ÷ 6 = 5 m s⁻². The 180 m s⁻² option multiplies the values instead.'),
('c901eb7d-04af-4268-a16c-bb4995497738', 'Gradient = (y₂ − y₁)/(x₂ − x₁) = (10 − 2)/(5 − 1) = 8/4 = 2. The −2 option reverses the x-subtraction but not the y-subtraction.'),
('caad985f-478a-4af1-8aca-eaae889e9557', 'P(X ≥ 1) = 1 − P(X = 0) = 1 − (0.5)⁸ = 1 − 1/256 ≈ 0.9961. Working from the complement avoids adding up the eight separate terms.'),
('cde43ad1-14fc-4abe-bb9b-6d6d05221add', 'The sum of an AP is Sₙ = n/2 × (2a + (n − 1)d). With n = 20, a = 2 and d = 3: S₂₀ = 10 × (4 + 57) = 610. The 600 option is close but is not the exact sum.'),
('ce48a38a-9729-4fa8-9c2a-75034e46f163', 'From y = (x − 10)/2 we get x = 2y + 10. The mean transforms in the same way, so x̄ = 2ȳ + 10 = 2 × 4 + 10 = 18.'),
('ceacf74b-a5c1-4022-abf2-c01b73c5b332', 'The standard error of the sample mean is σ/√n = 12/√36 = 12/6 = 2. The 0.33 option is σ/n, which divides by n rather than √n.'),
('cf83487f-999d-4264-8bc4-250dd9985ad4', 'Sector area is A = ½r²θ with θ in radians. Here A = ½ × 5² × 1.2 = ½ × 25 × 1.2 = 15. The 30 option forgets the one-half.'),
('d0132e03-3c00-45fc-b801-93331c43b654', 'Gravitational potential energy gain is Ep = mgh = 2 kg × 10 N/kg × 5 m = 100 J. The 20 J option leaves out the height.'),
('d0556755-706b-45c0-b553-bf5cb486c3c7', 'A JOIN combines rows from two or more tables where the key values match, which links related data across the tables. Sorting uses ORDER BY and filtering uses WHERE.'),
('d08d99c0-1687-4aff-9842-129ffee7b7b5', 'Integrate by parts with u = x and dv = e^x dx, so ∫x e^x dx = x e^x − ∫e^x dx = x e^x − e^x + c. Differentiating the answer confirms it.'),
('d27d7010-0b7a-4354-8b19-74babd770f30', 'The derivative of x² is 2x, so the gradient at x = 3 is 2 × 3 = 6. The 9 option is x² at x = 3, which is a height on the curve, not a gradient.'),
('d29501e5-7941-47eb-9eda-affd9621658e', 'A protocol is a set of agreed rules that govern how devices format, send and receive data. It is not a cable, a network topology or an operating system.'),
('d29d333d-6423-4080-bb59-b4fc1a010581', 'Text must be stored exactly, because a single changed character alters the meaning. Lossless compression keeps every bit, so it is the only safe choice for text.'),
('d4c89683-3f7c-41cc-8fa1-3c3a3d0cfd99', 'Work done is W = Fd when the force acts in the direction of motion: W = 20 N × 5 m = 100 J. The 25 J option adds the force and the distance.'),
('d5a9ad5f-de92-41fd-aa72-38f03ade0e41', 'The nth term is uₙ = a + (n − 1)d = 1 + (n − 1)2. Setting this to 21 gives 2(n − 1) = 20, so n − 1 = 10 and n = 11.'),
('d5ae382f-23d6-4b35-9c99-3c889d7efb7a', 'For a sinusoidal supply the RMS value is V_rms = V₀/√2 = 325/1.414 ≈ 230 V. The 325 V option is the peak value, not the RMS value.'),
('d7118973-229f-4556-a256-a6cdd6eb1680', 'Dividing by a fraction is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal: ⅔ ÷ ⅖ = ⅔ × 5/2 = 10/6 = 5/3.'),
('d87f3e3f-0afd-475e-afb6-ed98674e2474', 'Raise each factor to the power 2: (3x)² = 3² × x² = 9x². The 3x² option squares only the x and leaves the 3 unsquared.')
) as v(id, e)
where q.id = v.id::uuid;
